From e2f38b4f7fe90f95cc06b0989cf45bf9d0456985 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cDc <cdc.seacave@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 07:00:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Link pyOpenMVS to Python3::Module for the Python headers

Backport of the pyOpenMVS part of upstream commit e2f38b4 ("fixes:
consolidate contributor fixes for IO, texturing, and builds",
cdcseacave/openMVS#1294), which links pyOpenMVS to Python3::Module. That
change builds on cdcseacave/openMVS#1273 by Aljoscha Rheinwalt, which first
linked pyOpenMVS to Python's imported target and its include directories.

pyOpenMVS linked only MVS and ${Python3_LIBRARIES}, so it never got
Python3_INCLUDE_DIRS and compiled only when Python's headers happened to
be on another include path. Python 3.15 on Windows installs its headers in
include/python, where nothing else points.

Backported to 2.4.0 by Tobias Fischer <tobias.fischer@qut.edu.au>.

Co-authored-by: Aljoscha Rheinwalt <aljoscha.rheinwalt@uni-potsdam.de>
---
 libs/MVS/CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libs/MVS/CMakeLists.txt b/libs/MVS/CMakeLists.txt
index ac95177..87d31a8 100644
--- a/libs/MVS/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/libs/MVS/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@ if(OpenMVS_USE_PYTHON)
 	if(_USE_CUDA)
 		SET_TARGET_PROPERTIES(pyOpenMVS PROPERTIES CUDA_ARCHITECTURES "50;72;75")
 	endif()
-	TARGET_LINK_LIBRARIES(pyOpenMVS PRIVATE MVS)
+	TARGET_LINK_LIBRARIES(pyOpenMVS PRIVATE MVS Python3::Module)
 	# Suppress prefix "lib" because Python does not allow this prefix
 	SET_TARGET_PROPERTIES(pyOpenMVS PROPERTIES PREFIX "")
 	# Install
-- 
